(a) As used in this article, a "cigar store lounge" shall be defined as a retail establishment that derives over 51 percent of its total gross sales from handmade cigars based on the State of Georgia tax receipts and over 70 percent of its total gross sales from handmade cigars and other cigar-related products.
(b) Cigar store lounges, as defined herein, shall not sell or permit the use of:
(1) Vape products, including electronic smoking devices, component parts, or e-liquids;
(2) Cigarettes;
(3) Unrolled tobacco;
(4) Hookah products such as "hookas," glass pipes or bongs; and
(5) Machine rolled tobacco products.
(c) A cigar store lounge, as defined herein, may be eligible for a license for on-premise consumption of wine, malt beverages, and/or distilled spirits provided that such lounges meet all the requirements for a on-premise consumption licenses other than food requirements and such establishments meet the following requirements:
(1) Such establishment shall have a maximum capacity as determined by the fire marshall of 40 persons;
(2) Shall not be located within 500 yards of another cigar store lounge;
(3) Shall have a filtration system exceeding 98 percent efficiency;
(4) Shall meet all requirements of the State of Georgia regarding indoor smoking;
(5) Shall only sell or serve alcoholic beverages between the hours of 11:00 a.m. and 11:00 p.m. Monday through Saturday, and if authorized for Sunday sales, between the hours of 12:30 p.m. and 8:00 p.m. on Sundays.
(d) No alcoholic beverage license for on-premise consumption shall be issued to a cigar store lounge unless the establishment is located within the HT (historic town center) zoning district under the City of Senoia Zoning Ordinance.
(Ord. No. 24-07, § 3, 12-2-2024)
Editor's note— Ord. No. 24-07, §§ 3, 4, adopted Dec. 2, 2024, renumbered the former §§ 6-92—6-94 as §§ 6-94—6-96 and enacted new §§ 6-92 and 6-93 as set out herein. The historical notation has been retained with the amended provisions for reference purposes.

